Thanks for pushing back. I went the other way: instead of widening the docblocks to `array-key` and pushing `int|string` into your loop, `keys()` and the iterator now return the strings they always claimed, so `get($key)` works with no cast under strict_types. The annotations that describe what you pass in no longer constrain the key type, since the bag genuinely doesn't care.

all() still hands back the raw array, so numeric keys stay ints there; its annotation just doesn't claim otherwise any more. #66151 does the same for HeaderBag and the session bags.
